/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 324 0 R
/E (Fully Connected Layers are used at the final stage of a Convolutional Neural Network. In this layer, the feature maps extracted by the previous convolutional and pooling layers are flattened into a single one-dimensional vector. Every neuron in this layer is connected to every neuron in the next layer, allowing the network to combine all the learned features. Fully connected layers are responsible for making the final decision of the network, such as performing classification or regression based on the extracted features.)
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
